# Vendored ESP-IDF DHCP server

Source: components/lwip/apps/dhcpserver/dhcpserver.c
IDF version: 6.1.0
dhcpserver.c sha1: 4eba197c7fb2d76b

vendored_dhcps.c differs from upstream/dhcpserver.c only by:
  - renamed headers (guards __DHCPS_H__ -> __VENDORED_DHCPS_H__)
  - local fallbacks for MAX_STATION_NUM / LEASE_UNIT, which the IDF Kconfig
    removes when CONFIG_LWIP_DHCPS=n
  - `#if ESP_DHCPS` at the top of the file body replaced by VENDORED_DHCPS.
    ESP_DHCPS follows CONFIG_LWIP_DHCPS, so leaving it would compile this whole
    file to nothing with the IDF server disabled.
  - `#if CONFIG_LWIP_DHCPS` in dhcpserver.h likewise (it gates the per-client
    hostname storage)
  - static leases: a call to static_leases_lookup() in parse_msg(), inserted
    after POOL_CHECK and before parse_options() so that yiaddr (built by
    create_msg from dhcps->client_address) and the option-50 comparison both
    use the leased address. It overrides dhcps->client_address ONLY - writing
    the leased address into the pool entry as well silently breaks DHCP for
    that client (see the comment at the call site). Search for "local addition:
    static leases".

Run:  diff -u upstream/dhcpserver.c vendored_dhcps.c

The three files were copied on 2026-09-24 and have not been reconciled against
any later IDF release. When upgrading IDF, diff upstream/ against the new
components/lwip/apps/dhcpserver/ to see what was missed.
